# Cloudflare Pages headers: the security headers for every page, then a cache rule for /brand/ (below).
# CSP allows the inlined stylesheet
# (astro.config `inlineStylesheets: 'always'`) via style-src 'unsafe-inline' and
# the inline theme/analytics scripts. Widen script-src/connect-src only as needed.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Files under /brand/ keep their names when they change, and the Markdown snippets on /partner-assets
# hotlink the badges from partners' READMEs: cache them for a day, never mark them immutable. Pages'
# default is "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", which makes a cache ask the server before it reuses
# a file. Pages joins the values of one header set by several rules with a comma, so no other rule may
# set Cache-Control for these files; tests/navigation.spec.ts reads the result.
/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
